{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-j22f-vq7h-c4qm","cve_id":"CVE-2026-92708","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-j22f-vq7h-c4qm","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j22f-vq7h-c4qm","summary":"devalue: `stringify`/`uneval` serialize shared memory","description":"### Impact\n\n`stringify` and `uneval` serialize a typed array by emitting its backing `ArrayBuffer`, not just the view. In the case of a Node `Buffer` object, the backing buffer is a process-wide shared pool, meaning unrelated memory can be serialized into a response that is then sent to the client. For a Node `Buffer` the backing store is Node's **process-wide shared pool**, so serializing a small `Buffer` copies up to 64 KB of unrelated process memory — including bytes from other in-flight requests — into the output. In an SSR framework (SvelteKit, Nuxt) a public page whose `load()` returns a 2-byte `Buffer`, or a small file read with `readFileSync`, ships another user's request body / `Authorization` header in its HTML. Unauthenticated, silent, ~43,000× amplification.\n\nThis is serialization-side, so the `parse`/`unflatten` prototype-pollution and DoS guards do not apply — it fires on every SSR render, not only when parsing untrusted input.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nConvert Node `Buffer` objects to `Uint8Array`:\n\n```diff\npayload = {\n- buffer\n+ buffer: new Uint8Array(buffer)\n}\n```","type":"reviewed","severity":"high","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sveltejs/devalue/security-advisories/GHSA-j22f-vq7h-c4qm","source_code_location":"https://github.com/sveltejs/devalue","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-j22f-vq7h-c4qm","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-92708","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/sveltejs/devalue/security/advisories/GHSA-j22f-vq7h-c4qm","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-92708","https://github.com/sveltejs/devalue/commit/46dc877b3570dafb1cd3291b9bb48cecef8f7266","https://github.com/sveltejs/devalue/releases/tag/v5.9.3","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j22f-vq7h-c4qm"],"published_at":"2026-10-01T15:18:06Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T15:18:07Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-10-01T15:18:06Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-09-18T20:17:30Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"devalue"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 5.1.0, <= 5.9.2","first_patched_version":"5.9.3","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N","score":7.5},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-200","name":"Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor"},{"cwe_id":"CWE-226","name":"Sensitive Information in Resource Not Removed Before Reuse"}],"credits":[{"user":{"login":"LipezJ","id":89532423,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5NTMyNDIz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89532423?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LipezJ","html_url":"https://github.com/LipezJ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LipezJ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LipezJ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LipezJ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LipezJ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LipezJ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LipezJ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LipezJ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LipezJ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LipezJ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"reporter"},{"user":{"login":"elliott-with-the-longest-name-on-github","id":76245373,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MjQ1Mzcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76245373?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliott-with-the-longest-name-on-github","html_url":"https://github.com/elliott-with-the-longest-name-on-git